  "with_a_build_before_a_level": "builds beside their levels 9.1 s against 9.3 s alone (97 %), 23 % of one box; CPU 129 s against 136 s (95 %)"
 },
 "reading": "The work is not multiplied: the workers' CPU for a whole first visit is 531 to 593 s at every pool size. What grows with the pool is the tasks' wall time (556 s with one box, 1,300 s with eight on four cores): a task waiting for a core counts as busy, which is what the Mac's count summed. About 150 s of the work is the 396 builds; about 400 s is level-making, nearly all of it 12 tree kinds outside (and 15 inside) that have no levels of their own and are simplified from 0.5 to 1.7 million triangles, 12 to 94 s a kind. Each turn a build gives back goes to a waiting level job first (the box asks for its next turn a moment later), so the level jobs take every turn and the builds the world waits for stand still behind them."
